# RC-89: generated audit artifacts carry absolute operator-home paths, so the credential-leak
# hook rejects them on every commit. They were unstaged by hand three times on 2026-07-27 —
# fixing the instance instead of the cause. They are regenerated output, never source.
governance/audits/

# RC-89 pattern: generated stream artifacts embed the absolute repo path, so the
# credential-leak hook rejects them on every commit. They are regenerable output, never
# source. (The locks_* audit tools and their reports were removed in the 2026-08-24
# teardown; the ignore rows keep any stale local outputs unstaged.)
reports/locks_inventory_v1.json
reports/locks_violation_audit_v1.json
reports/locks_violation_monitor_v1.json
reports/locks_violation_monitor_prev_v1.json
reports/stream_raw_sample_*.json
reports/stream_capture_status.json

# RC-101: the scorecard artifacts are COMMITTED again — run_provenance now records the
# interpreter repo-relatively, so the artifacts carry no home paths. Only the run log stays
# ignored (it is a log). Gitignoring the artifacts was treating the symptom: it left a fresh
# clone with NO coach data while a local leftover silently served the API.
reports/scorecard_run.log

# runtime measurement log (RC-54 producer) - grows every session, never a repo artifact
reports/flip_drift_log.jsonl
# RC-251: append-only per-run TQM telemetry. The reviewable artifacts are
# reports/rehab_latest.md and reports/tqm_queue_latest.json, which ARE tracked.
reports/rehab_queue.jsonl
# The raw machine dump embeds absolute operator-home paths and verbatim mission text
# (the credential-leak hook refused it, correctly). The markdown carries the same findings.
reports/rehab_latest.json

# RC-263: scratch has no lifecycle. 7,793 tracked files / 485,275,039 bytes -- 75% of the
# repository -- was throwaway debugging output, including six committed Chrome browser
# profiles and a 98.5%-identical second copy of server.py. Nothing imports it; the only
# reference outside it is a docstring citation in math_levels.py. Untracked 2026-08-06.
# Files stay on disk; git history retains them. Nothing here may be imported by production.
scratchpad/
